# Review ownership for the release path and the tooling that drives it.
#
# GitHub consults this file ONLY when it evaluates a pull request's reviews, and ONLY from the
# branch that pull request TARGETS -- never from the default branch. On its own it blocks
# nothing: what gives it force is whichever org ruleset applies to THIS branch, and that is a
# separate object that changes over time. A copy missing from one branch protects nothing there
# and fails SILENTLY, by requesting no review at all, which is why the file exists on each of
# the three branches separately and is kept identical across them.
#
# WHAT THE PATHS BELOW MEAN, as of 2026-09-18. The operator's branch policy requires an admin
# for any pull request into `dev` that touches CI or scripts, and requires an admin to merge
# into `test` or `prod` at all. This file is the whole implementation of the first half:
# there is no ruleset field for "CI or scripts", so the guarded set is exactly what is listed
# here. A path absent from this list is a path any developer may change and merge alone on
# `dev`. On `test` and `prod` the admin-merge ruleset already refuses a non-admin.
#
# It is deliberately BROAD -- all of `/scripts/`, not a subdirectory of it.
#
# There are three branches and only three. `main` was deleted on the remote on 2026-08-21 in
# every repository on this model.
#
# Owner: scripts/apply-codeowners.mjs in infra-control-plane, which DERIVES this file from
# the repo's own previous copy rather than rendering a template.

